            "time": "2026-10-20T22:35:17Z",
            "attachment_id": 3933,
            "count": 0,
            "text": "Created attachment 3933\ncacheMetadata and ..checkRequiredGenerics handle duplicates correctly\n\nThere are two minor logic bugs in `methods::cacheMetaData()` surrounding handling of duplicates\n\n1. `duplicate()` is run independently for `package` and `generic`\n2. We prune the duplicates only for the `generic` object but not the paired `package`\n\nThe attached bug handles this, and also cleans up the storage type of the `.NeedPrimitiveMethods` which is currently `list`, which is a bit more complicated to work with where plain `character` will suffice. NB: for simplicity, this patch is written with a new major release (e.g. 4.7.0) in mind, where we can assume existing `.requireCachedGenerics` list objects in pre-compiled namespaces needn't be accommodated.\n\nThe patch also reaches for the convenient `get0()` over `if (exists(...)) get(...)` in a number of places, and includes an early return refactoring. These grow the patch beyond something strictly minimal, but I think are manageable.\n\nI didn't find any packages affected by this -- the fact that `package` is most often simply `\"base\"` is a saving grace -- but we _can_ see the benefit of deduplication in `..checkRequiredGenerics` immediately, e.g. {Rcpp} currently has:\n\n```\nRcpp:::.requireCachedGenerics\n# [[1]]\n# [1] \"$\"\n\n# [[2]]\n# [1] \"$<-\"\n\n# [[3]]\n# [1] \"$\"\n\n# [[4]]\n# [1] \"$<-\"\n\n# [[5]]\n# [1] \"$\"\n\n# [[6]]\n# [1] \"$<-\"\n\n# [[7]]\n# [1] \"Ops\"\n\n# [[8]]\n# [1] \"$\"\n\n# [[9]]\n# [1] \"$<-\"\n\n# attr(,\"package\")\n# [1] \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\" \"base\"\n```\n\nWhich this patch would instead simplify to:\n\n```\n# [1] \"$\"   \"$<-\" \"Ops\"\n# attr(,\"package\")\n# [1] \"base\" \"base\" \"base\"\n```\n\nAs to the bug, courtesy LLM, here is a toy example that doesn't require writing out all the test package sources:\n\n```\nmk_ns <- function(name) {\n  ns <- new.env(parent=.GlobalEnv)\n  ns$.packageName <- name\n  .Internal(registerNamespace(name, ns))\n  ns\n}\nPkgA <- mk_ns(\"PkgA\")\nPkgB <- mk_ns(\"PkgB\")\nPkgC <- mk_ns(\"PkgC\")\n\ninvisible({\nsetGeneric(\"bar\", \\(x) standardGeneric(\"bar\"), where=PkgB)\nsetGeneric(\"foo\", \\(x) standardGeneric(\"foo\"), where=PkgA)\nsetGeneric(\"foo\", \\(x) standardGeneric(\"foo\"), where=PkgB)\nsetGeneric(\"zzz\", \\(x) standardGeneric(\"zzz\"), where=PkgC)\n})\n\n# PkgD defines a class and methods on all 4 generics:\nPkgD <- mk_ns(\"PkgD\")\nsetClass(\"MyClass\", slots=c(x=\"numeric\"), where = PkgD)\nsetMethod(PkgB$bar, \"MyClass\", \\(x) \"PkgB::bar\", where=PkgD)\nsetMethod(PkgA$foo, \"MyClass\", \\(x) \"PkgA::foo\", where=PkgD)\nsetMethod(PkgB$foo, \"MyClass\", \\(x) \"PkgB::foo\", where=PkgD)\nsetMethod(PkgC$zzz, \"MyClass\", \\(x) \"PkgC::zzz\", where=PkgD)\n\n# Simulate fresh package load: uncache methods, then run cacheMetaData(PkgD, TRUE)\nfor (g in list(PkgB$bar, PkgA$foo, PkgB$foo, PkgC$zzz)) {\n  methods:::.updateMethodsInTable(g, PkgD, attach=FALSE)\n}\ncacheMetaData(PkgD, attach = TRUE)\n\n# Test dispatch on all 4 generics:\nx <- new(\"MyClass\", x=1)\nPkgB$bar(x) # [1] \"PkgB::bar\"\nPkgA$foo(x) # [1] \"PkgA::foo\"\ntry(PkgB$foo(x))\ntry(PkgC$zzz(x))\n```\n\nErrors on the last two:\n\n```\nError : unable to find an inherited method for function 'foo' for signature 'x = \"MyClass\"'\nError : unable to find an inherited method for function 'zzz' for signature 'x = \"MyClass\"'\n```\n\nI've left this patch without tests, as I'm still not sure the preferred style for regression tests requiring test packages such as here. With some guidance I can write some tests to spec.",
